{"id": "3696715c-b330-4bbb-aa43-9043cee11ce2", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll apply the DynamoDB latency analysis methodology to this scenario for you.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_DlhDZjwtib13AASAjnoYXJ", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Classify a hypothetical DynamoDB latency scenario using the DynamoDB latency analysis skill/runbook, and explain the likely cause of the Scan slowdown. This is a hypothetical exercise — do NOT make any AWS calls; use only the data provided below.",
  "context": "User is reasoning about a nightly batch job on table 'reports-prod' (on-demand capacity mode) that uses a Scan operation. They want to know: (1) whether a Scan p50 of 410ms is actually 'slow' for a Scan operation, and (2) what likely caused the increase from the 7-day baseline.",
  "resources": ["reports-prod (DynamoDB table, on-demand)"],
  "timeframe": "14-day window, 300-second (5-minute) periods, compared against a 7-day baseline",
  "criteria": "Provided metrics (treat as ground truth, no further data needed):\n- Operation: Scan (used by the nightly job)\n- Scan p50 latency: 410 ms (current) vs 120 ms (7-day baseline)\n- Latency elevated in 62% of assessable periods\n- Every period has hundreds of requests (so sample size is not a concern)\n- ReturnedItemCount for Scan: averaged 980 items/request (current) vs 310 items/request (baseline)\n- Mean item size (TableSizeBytes/ItemCount): 148 KB\n- No errors or throttling recorded\n\nApply the DynamoDB latency skill's classification logic (e.g. is this latency level expected/abnormal for a Scan given item count and size returned per request, what category of root cause this points to — e.g. payload growth / data growth driving larger result sets per Scan page, vs capacity throttling, vs network, vs partition issues) and return: (a) a verdict on whether 410ms is 'slow' in context, (b) the most likely root cause category with supporting reasoning tying together the ReturnedItemCount increase (980 vs 310) and 148KB mean item size, (c) whether throttling/errors are ruled in or out as a cause, (d) suggested classification label the skill would assign."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Apply DynamoDB latency classification methodology to hypothetical scan latency scenario, no AWS calls."}], "created_at": null}
